---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Harness Engineering"
  description="Eric Nolan's evidence-driven work on the systems surrounding AI models: context, memory, tools, governance, orchestration, verification, and bounded automation."
>
  <header class="subhero subhero--harness">
    <div class="shell subhero-grid">
      <div class="subhero-copy">
        <div class="subhero-badges">
          <span>AI SYSTEMS</span>
          <span>RUNTIME DESIGN</span>
          <span>GOVERNANCE</span>
        </div>
        <p class="subhero-kicker">HARNESS ENGINEERING // SYSTEMS AROUND THE MODEL</p>
        <h1>The model is not the product.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Context, memory, instructions, tools, routing, state, evaluation, approval, and execution boundaries determine what an AI system can know, do, and recover from.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button button-pop" href="https://github.com/unyieldingclaw-dev/harness-engineering">Open the research repo →</a>
          <a class="button secondary case-secondary" href="#framework">Explore the framework ↓</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div
        class="harness-map"
        id="system-map"
        tabindex="0"
        data-trail-hover="harness-sag"
        aria-label="Harness Engineering system map. Context, memory, tools, orchestration, governance, evaluation, and runtime surround the model."
      >
        <button class="harness-core egg-mark egg-mark--dark matrix-trigger" type="button" data-matrix-trigger data-egg="PROMPTING ≠ ARCHITECTURE" aria-label="Model node. Open the Matrix easter egg." aria-describedby="model-egg-clue">MODEL</button>
        <span class="sr-only" id="model-egg-clue">Hidden note: prompting is not architecture.</span>
        <div class="harness-node node-context"><span>CONTEXT</span><small>authority · freshness</small></div>
        <div class="harness-node node-memory"><span>MEMORY</span><small>state · provenance</small></div>
        <div class="harness-node node-tools"><span>TOOLS</span><small>contracts · permissions</small></div>
        <div class="harness-node node-orchestration"><span>ORCHESTRATION</span><small>routing · handoffs</small></div>
        <div class="harness-node node-governance"><span>GOVERNANCE</span><small>scope · approval</small></div>
        <div class="harness-node node-evaluation"><span>EVALUATION</span><small>evidence · behavior</small></div>
        <div class="harness-node node-runtime"><span>RUNTIME</span><small>retries · recovery</small></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section harness-thesis" id="framework">
    <div class="shell thesis-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The thesis</p>
        <h2>Prompt quality is not enough.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="thesis-copy">
        <p>
          AI products collect stuff fast: prompts, rules, memory, tools, routers, evaluators, retries, approval gates, and whatever somebody added Friday afternoon to stop the last incident from happening again.
        </p>
        <p>
          Harness Engineering is where I work through how that surrounding layer should fit together—and which parts do not deserve to exist yet.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--dark harness-principles">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading section-heading--punch">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Current research themes</p>
          <h2>Where the hard questions live.</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="section-intro">These are the questions I keep running into when the demo is over and the system has to behave.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="harness-question-grid">
        <article class="harness-question">
          <span>01 // CONTEXT</span>
          <h3>Which source wins?</h3>
          <p>When instructions, project memory, runtime evidence, and user intent disagree, authority needs an explicit order.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="harness-question">
          <span>02 // EXECUTION</span>
          <h3>What should the model be allowed to do?</h3>
          <p>Automation should have bounded authority, deterministic stops, and approval gates where consequences deserve judgment.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="harness-question">
          <span>03 // VERIFICATION</span>
          <h3>Who checks the checker?</h3>
          <p>Independent evidence matters. The same reasoning path should not be the only authority judging its own output.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="harness-question">
          <span>04 // OBSERVABILITY</span>
          <h3>What evidence already exists?</h3>
          <p>Do not install telemetry because the diagram looks incomplete. Measure the real gap before adding machinery.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section harness-rule">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="rule-card">
        <button class="trail-marker trail-marker--harness" type="button" data-trail-marker="harness-trail" aria-label="Hidden trail marker: Systems Trail">◇</button>
        <span class="rule-card__index">RULE 001</span>
        <blockquote>No new machinery without an observed need.</blockquote>
        <p>
          Use deterministic sources where they already exist. Measure first. Add agents, telemetry, or infrastructure only when an observed failure mode earns the complexity.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div
    class="matrix-overlay"
    data-matrix-overlay
    role="dialog"
    aria-modal="true"
    aria-labelledby="matrix-title"
    aria-describedby="matrix-description"
    aria-hidden="true"
    inert
  >
    <canvas class="matrix-canvas" data-matrix-canvas aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
    <div class="matrix-overlay__message">
      <span>HARNESS ENGINEERING // RUNTIME CHECK</span>
      <strong id="matrix-title">THE MODEL IS NOT THE PRODUCT.</strong>
      <small id="matrix-description">There is no spoon. There is, however, a tool contract.</small>
    </div>
    <button type="button" class="matrix-overlay__close" data-matrix-close aria-label="Close Matrix easter egg">ESC</button>
  </div>

  <script is:inline>
    (() => {
      const trigger = document.querySelector('[data-matrix-trigger]');
      const overlay = document.querySelector('[data-matrix-overlay]');
      const canvas = document.querySelector('[data-matrix-canvas]');
      const close = document.querySelector('[data-matrix-close]');
      if (!trigger || !overlay || !canvas) return;

      const reduceMotion = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
      const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
      let animationFrame;
      let stopTimer;
      let running = false;
      let neoBuffer = '';
      let previousFocus = null;

      const sizeCanvas = () => {
        const dpr = Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio || 1, 2);
        canvas.width = Math.floor(window.innerWidth * dpr);
        canvas.height = Math.floor(window.innerHeight * dpr);
        canvas.style.width = window.innerWidth + 'px';
        canvas.style.height = window.innerHeight + 'px';
        ctx.setTransform(dpr, 0, 0, dpr, 0, 0);
      };

      const stopMatrix = ({ restoreFocus = true } = {}) => {
        running = false;
        cancelAnimationFrame(animationFrame);
        clearTimeout(stopTimer);
        overlay.classList.remove('is-active');
        overlay.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
        overlay.inert = true;

        if (restoreFocus && previousFocus instanceof HTMLElement) {
          previousFocus.focus({ preventScroll: true });
        }
      };

      const startMatrix = () => {
        if (running) return;
        window.unyieldingTrailDiscover?.('harness-matrix', 'MATRIX FOUND');
        previousFocus = document.activeElement;
        running = true;
        overlay.inert = false;
        overlay.classList.add('is-active');
        overlay.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'false');
        close?.focus({ preventScroll: true });

        if (reduceMotion) {
          stopTimer = setTimeout(stopMatrix, 2600);
          return;
        }

        sizeCanvas();
        const fontSize = 17;
        let columns = Math.ceil(window.innerWidth / fontSize);
        let drops = Array(columns).fill(0).map(() => Math.random() * -40);

        const draw = () => {
          if (!running) return;
          ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(0, 8, 4, 0.11)';
          ctx.fillRect(0, 0, window.innerWidth, window.innerHeight);
          ctx.fillStyle = '#53ff8a';
          ctx.font = fontSize + 'px ui-monospace, monospace';

          for (let i = 0; i < drops.length; i++) {
            const text = Math.random() > 0.5 ? '1' : '0';
            ctx.fillText(text, i * fontSize, drops[i] * fontSize);
            if (drops[i] * fontSize > window.innerHeight && Math.random() > 0.975) drops[i] = 0;
            drops[i] += 0.75 + Math.random() * 0.35;
          }

          animationFrame = requestAnimationFrame(draw);
        };

        ctx.fillStyle = '#000';
        ctx.fillRect(0, 0, window.innerWidth, window.innerHeight);
        draw();
        stopTimer = setTimeout(stopMatrix, 5200);
      };

      trigger.addEventListener('click', startMatrix);
      close?.addEventListener('click', stopMatrix);
      overlay.addEventListener('click', (event) => {
        if (event.target === overlay || event.target === canvas) stopMatrix();
      });

      document.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {
        if (running && event.key === 'Tab') {
          event.preventDefault();
          close?.focus();
          return;
        }

        if (event.key === 'Escape' && running) {
          stopMatrix();
          return;
        }
        const target = event.target;
        if (target instanceof HTMLInputElement || target instanceof HTMLTextAreaElement || target?.isContentEditable) return;
        if (event.key.length !== 1) return;
        neoBuffer = (neoBuffer + event.key.toLowerCase()).slice(-3);
        if (neoBuffer === 'neo') {
          startMatrix();
          neoBuffer = '';
        }
      });

      window.addEventListener('resize', () => {
        if (running && !reduceMotion) sizeCanvas();
      }, { passive: true });
    })();
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
